## "er1600"
## an rz1600 emulator.

## <https://www.github.com/quxrzd/er1600>


## ABOUT
"er1600" is a rezoid(tm) rz1600 cycle-accurate emulator
implemented as a C++ library.


## COMPILE
er1600 requires a C++11 compiler and make.
"all", "run", and "clr" targets can be used.

on a unix-like machine, run the following:
$ make -f mkf <target>

replace <target> with the target of choice. 


## HACKING
to hack around, simply copy the src/er1600 directory and
implement it in your own projects.

"microcode.c++" is the file with the microcode
implementations defined in "er1600.h++", in which
"er1600.c++" puts to use. "prg.c++" is a dummy program.


